Okay, with `0.4.0` there is a different failure. Bevy will compile with `0.4.0` but, it will fail when using `DefaultPlugins` or `MinimalPlugins`. However, the following code will not crash(but will fail to run):

```
use bevy::core::CorePlugin;
use app::{PluginGroupBuilder, ScheduleRunnerPlugin};
use bevy::*;
use bevy::prelude::*;
use reflect::ReflectPlugin;
pub struct my_plug;

impl PluginGroup for my_plug {
    fn build(&mut self, group: &mut PluginGroupBuilder) {
    }
}

fn main() {
    App::build()
    .add_plugin(CorePlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(ScheduleRunnerPlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(ReflectPlugin::default())
    .add_plugins(my_plug)
    .add_startup_system(my_start.system())
    .run();
}

fn my_start() {
    println!("Hey!");
}
```

I must be doing something wrong with adding individual plugins, because first the previous code will compile, but crashes when run (both 64 and 32 bit (`thread 'main' panicked at 'called 'Option::unwrap()' on a 'None' value'`)). If I exchange the individual adding of plugins with `.add_plugins(MinimalPlugins)`. However, when running in 64-bit the previous code will work and 32-bit will fail to compile completely.

Here we go again. The following compiles and runs without error:

```
use asset::AssetPlugin;
use bevy::{core::CorePlugin, window::WindowPlugin};
use app::{PluginGroupBuilder, ScheduleRunnerPlugin};
use bevy::*;
use bevy::prelude::*;
use diagnostic::DiagnosticsPlugin;
use input::InputPlugin;
use log::LogPlugin;
use reflect::ReflectPlugin;
use scene::ScenePlugin;

pub struct MyPlug;

impl PluginGroup for MyPlug {
    fn build(&mut self, group: &mut PluginGroupBuilder) {
        group.add(MyPlug);
    }
}
impl Plugin for MyPlug {
    fn build(&self, _: &mut AppBuilder) {

    }
}

fn main() {
    App::build()
    .add_plugin(LogPlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(ReflectPlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(CorePlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(TransformPlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(DiagnosticsPlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(InputPlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(WindowPlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(AssetPlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(ScenePlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(ScheduleRunnerPlugin::default())
    .add_plugin(MyPlug)
    .add_plugins(MyPlug)
    .add_startup_system(my_start.system())
    .run();
}

fn my_start() {
    println!("Hey!");
}
```
However, replacing all of the `add_plugin(s)` with `.add_plugins(MinimalPlugins)` creates a link error. Though, it does not fail with my custom `PluginGroup`. Also, despite adding all of these plugins, I still do not receive a window. Also, when using `add_plugin(RenderPlugin::default()` the linker crashes.

